{
 "unidades": [
  {
   "id": "u04",
   "titulo": {
    "en": "Stress and the tilde"
   },
   "objetivo": {
    "en": "Find the strong syllable of a word, use the two basic stress rules, read words with a tilde, and read ¿ and ¡."
   },
   "lecciones": [
    {
     "id": "u04.l01",
     "titulo": {
      "en": "The strong syllable"
     },
     "pasos": [
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "anima",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Every Spanish word has one syllable that you say louder and longer: the strong syllable. Here it is written in capitals, like ME-sa."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "m(e:e)(s:s)(a:a)",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Me-sa: the strong syllable is ME. Say ME-sa, not me-SA."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Rule 1: words that end in a vowel, n or s are strong on the second-to-last syllable: ME-sa, a-MI-go, CO-men, LU-nes."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(a:a)m(i:i)(g:g)(o:o)",
         "t": {
          "en": "friend · a-MI-go"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(o:o)m(e:e)n",
         "t": {
          "en": "they eat · CO-men"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "l(u:u)n(e:e)(s:s)",
         "t": {
          "en": "Monday · LU-nes"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "l(i:i)(b:b)(r:r)(o:o)(s:s)",
         "e": "1f4da",
         "t": {
          "en": "books · LI-bros"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(z:s)(a:a)p(a:a)t(o:o)",
         "e": "1f45e",
         "t": {
          "en": "shoe · za-PA-to"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "(z:s)(a:a)p(a:a)t(o:o)",
       "t": {
        "en": "shoe"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which syllable is strong?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "(z:s)(a:a)"
        },
        {
         "m": "t(o:o)"
        },
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 2
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "(a:a)m(i:i)(g:g)(o:o)",
       "t": {
        "en": "friend"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which syllable is strong?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "m(i:i)"
        },
        {
         "m": "(a:a)"
        },
        {
         "m": "(g:g)(o:o)"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 0
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Rule 2: words that end in any other consonant are strong on the last syllable: ho-TEL, a-ni-MAL, re-LOJ, co-LOR."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(h:_)(o:o)t(e:e)l",
         "e": "1f3e8",
         "t": {
          "en": "hotel · ho-TEL"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(a:a)n(i:i)m(a:a)l",
         "e": "1f43e",
         "t": {
          "en": "animal · a-ni-MAL"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(r:rr)(e:e)l(o:o)(j:jota)",
         "e": "231a",
         "t": {
          "en": "watch · re-LOJ"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(e:e)l",
         "e": "1f4c4",
         "t": {
          "en": "paper · pa-PEL"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(o:o)l(o:o)(r:r)",
         "e": "1f3a8",
         "t": {
          "en": "color · co-LOR"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "p(a:a)p(e:e)l",
       "t": {
        "en": "paper"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which syllable is strong?"
       },
       "opciones": [
