    {
     "id": "u04.l02",
     "titulo": {
      "en": "The tilde: when the rule breaks"
     },
     "pasos": [
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "anima",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Some words do not follow the two rules. Then Spanish writes a tilde (´) over the strong vowel. If you see a tilde, that vowel is the strong one. Always."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "(c:k)(a:a)f(é:e)",
       "sonido": "e",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Café ends in a vowel, so rule 1 would say CA-fe. But the tilde on é says ca-FÉ. The tilde wins."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(a:a)f(é:e)",
         "e": "2615",
         "t": {
          "en": "coffee · ca-FÉ"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(á:a)",
         "e": "1f468",
         "t": {
          "en": "dad · pa-PÁ"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "m(a:a)m(á:a)",
         "e": "1f469",
         "t": {
          "en": "mom · ma-MÁ"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(s:s)(o:o)f(á:a)",
         "e": "1f6cb",
         "t": {
          "en": "couch · so-FÁ"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "(a:a)(v:b)(i:i)(ó:o)n",
       "sonido": "o",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Avión ends in n, so rule 1 would say A-vion. The tilde moves the strength to the end: a-VIÓN."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(a:a)(v:b)(i:i)(ó:o)n",
         "e": "2708",
         "t": {
          "en": "airplane · a-VIÓN"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(a:a)n(c:s)(i:i)(ó:o)n",
         "e": "1f3b6",
         "t": {
          "en": "song · can-CIÓN"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "t(e:e)l(é:e)f(o:o)n(o:o)",
         "e": "260e",
         "t": {
          "en": "phone · te-LÉ-fo-no"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "pl(á:a)t(a:a)n(o:o)",
         "e": "1f34c",
         "t": {
          "en": "banana (plantain in some countries) · PLÁ-ta-no"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "(á:a)(r:r)(b:b)(o:o)l",
       "sonido": "a",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Árbol ends in l, so rule 2 would say ar-BOL. The tilde moves the strength to the front: ÁR-bol."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(á:a)(r:r)(b:b)(o:o)l",
         "e": "1f333",
         "t": {
          "en": "tree · ÁR-bol"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "l(á:a)p(i:i)(z:s)",
         "e": "270f",
         "t": {
          "en": "pencil · LÁ-piz"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "m(ú:u)(s:s)(i:i)(c:k)(a:a)",
         "e": "1f3b5",
         "t": {
          "en": "music · MÚ-si-ca"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Spanish has names for the three patterns. Aguda: strong on the last syllable (ca-FÉ, ho-TEL). Llana: strong on the second-to-last (ME-sa, ÁR-bol). Esdrújula: strong on the third-to-last (MÚ-si-ca, te-LÉ-fo-no). An esdrújula always carries a tilde."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Watch out: papa (PA-pa) is a potato, and papá (pa-PÁ) is dad. The letters are almost the same; only the tilde and the strong syllable change."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha_elige",
       "audio": "papá",
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which one did you hear?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(a:a)",
         "e": "1f954"
        },
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(á:a)",
         "e": "1f468"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 1
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha_elige",
       "audio": "papa",
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which one did you hear?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(a:a)",
         "e": "1f954"
        },
        {
         "m": "p(a:a)p(á:a)",
         "e": "1f468"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 0
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "m(ú:u)(s:s)(i:i)(c:k)(a:a)",
       "t": {
        "en": "music"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which syllable is strong?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "m(ú:u)"
        },
        {
         "m": "(s:s)(i:i)"
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(a:a)"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 0
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "(c:k)(a:a)n(c:s)(i:i)(ó:o)n",
       "t": {
        "en": "song"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Which syllable is strong?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "(c:s)(i:i)(ó:o)n"
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(a:a)n"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 0
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "A tilde can also tell two similar words apart: si (if) and sí (yes), tu (your) and tú (you), el (the) and él (he)."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(s:s)(í:i)",
         "t": {
          "en": "yes"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(s:s)(i:i)",
         "t": {
          "en": "if"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "t(ú:u)",
         "t": {
          "en": "you"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "t(u:u)",
         "t": {
          "en": "your"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(é:e)l",
         "t": {
          "en": "he"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(e:e)l",
         "t": {
          "en": "the"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "construye",
       "m": "(a:a)(v:b)(i:i)(ó:o)n",
       "fichas": [
        "a",
        "v",
        "i",
        "ó",
        "n",
        "o",
        "i"
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "repite",
       "m": "M(a:a)m(á:a) (y:i) p(a:a)p(á:a)",
       "t": {
        "en": "Mom and Dad"
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u04.l03",
     "titulo": {
      "en": "Questions and exclamations: ¿ ¡"
     },
     "pasos": [
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "sorprendido",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Spanish opens questions and exclamations with upside-down marks: ¿ and ¡. They warn you from the first word that a question or an exclamation is coming. A yes/no question rises at the end; an exclamation gets extra energy."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "¿(C:k)(ó:o)m(o:o) (e:e)(s:s)t(á:a)(s:s)?",
       "texto": {
        "en": "The ¿ opens the question and the ? closes it. Cómo estás means how are you."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "¡(Qu:k)(é:e) (r:rr)(i:i)(c:k)(o:o)!",
       "texto": {
        "en": "The ¡ opens an exclamation and the ! closes it. Say it with energy. Qué rico means how delicious."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "pensando",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Question words carry a tilde when they ask a question or begin an exclamation: qué (what), cómo (how), dónde (where), quién (who). The tilde lets you tell them from que (that), como (as, like), donde (where, in a statement), quien (who, in a statement)."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(qu:k)(é:e)",
         "t": {
          "en": "what"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(ó:o)m(o:o)",
         "t": {
          "en": "how"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(d:d)(ó:o)n(d:d)(e:e)",
         "t": {
          "en": "where · DÓN-de"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(qu:k)(i:i)(é:e)n",
         "t": {
          "en": "who · quién"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "¿(C:k)(ó:o)m(o:o) (e:e)(s:s)t(á:a)(s:s)?",
         "t": {
          "en": "How are you?"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "¿(D:d)(ó:o)n(d:d)(e:e) (v:b)(i:i)(v:b)(e:e) (E:e)mm(a:a)?",
         "t": {
          "en": "Where does Emma live?"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "¡M(u:u)(y:i) (b:b)(i:i)(e:e)n!",
         "t": {
          "en": "Very well!"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "¡(Qu:k)(é:e) (r:rr)(i:i)(c:k)(o:o)!",
         "t": {
          "en": "How delicious!"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "¿(D:d)(ó:o)n(d:d)(e:e) (v:b)(i:i)(v:b)(e:e) (E:e)mm(a:a)?",
       "t": {
        "en": "Where does Emma live?"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Is it a question or an exclamation?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "e": "2757"
        },
        {
         "e": "2753"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 1
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "¡(Qu:k)(é:e) (r:rr)(i:i)(c:k)(o:o)!",
       "t": {
        "en": "How delicious!"
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Is it a question or an exclamation?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "e": "2757"
        },
        {
         "e": "2753"
        }
       ],
       "correcta": 0
      },
      {
       "tipo": "lee",
       "m": "(E:e)mm(a:a) (v:b)(i:i)(v:b)(e:e) (e:e)n (Qu:k)(i:i)t(o:o).",
       "t": {
        "en": "Emma lives in Quito."
       },
       "pregunta": {
        "en": "Where does Emma live?"
       },
       "opciones": [
        {
         "m": "L(i:i)m(a:a)"
        },
        {
         "m": "(Qu:k)(i:i)t(o:o)"
        }
