  {
   "id": "u05",
   "titulo": {
    "en": "Diphthongs and the final test"
   },
   "objetivo": {
    "en": "Read two vowels in one beat (ai, ei, oi, au, eu, ie, ue, ua, io), tell them apart from two separate beats, and show that you can read Spanish."
   },
   "lecciones": [
    {
     "id": "u05.l01",
     "titulo": {
      "en": "Two vowels, one beat (1)"
     },
     "pasos": [
      {
       "tipo": "lumo",
       "pose": "anima",
       "texto": {
        "en": "In Spanish, a, e and o are strong vowels; i and u are weak. When a weak vowel sits next to a strong one, they share one beat: a diphthong. Each vowel keeps its pure sound; the weak one is just quick."
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "mira",
       "m": "(a:a)(i:i)(r:r)(e:e)",
       "sonido": "a",
       "texto": {
        "en": "Aire is a quick \"ah\" plus a quick \"ee\" in one beat. It sounds close to the English word \"eye\": EYE-reh. Aire means air. (Likewise ei is close to the ay in day, and oi to the oy in boy.)"
       }
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(a:a)(i:i)(r:r)(e:e)",
         "e": "1f32c",
         "t": {
          "en": "air, wind"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(b:b)(a:a)(i:i)l(e:e)",
         "e": "1f483",
         "t": {
          "en": "dance"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(c:k)(a:a)(i:i)m(á:a)n",
         "e": "1f40a",
         "t": {
          "en": "caiman"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(r:rr)(e:e)(i:i)n(a:a)",
         "e": "1f478",
         "t": {
          "en": "queen"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "tipo": "escucha",
       "palabras": [
        {
         "m": "(v:b)(e:e)(i:i)nt(e:e)",
         "t": {
          "en": "twenty"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "p(e:e)(i:i)n(e:e)",
         "t": {
          "en": "comb"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(h:_)(o:o)(y:i)",
         "e": "1f4c5",
         "t": {
          "en": "today"
         }
        },
        {
         "m": "(v:b)(o:o)(y:i)",
         "t": {
          "en": "I go"
         }
        }
       ]
      },
